<%- include('../partials/header') %>
<div class="page-head"><div><h1>Data export</h1><p class="sub">Download a copy of all records for safekeeping or to move to another system.</p></div></div>
<div class="row g-3" style="max-width: 1000px;">
  <div class="col-lg-7">
    <div class="panel"><div class="panel-body">
      <h2 class="panel-title">What is included</h2>
      <table class="table table-compact mb-3">
        <tbody>
        <% for (const [name, n] of Object.entries(counts)) { %><tr><td><%= name %></td><td class="num-col"><%= n %></td></tr><% } %>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="small text-body-secondary">Passwords and two-step verification secrets are never exported. Attached files are not included; they stay in storage and are listed by name.</p>
      <form method="post" action="/admin/export" data-confirm="This file contains confidential client information. Store it securely and delete it when no longer needed. Continue?">
        <%- f.hidden(csrfToken) %>
        <button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit" data-keep><i class="bi bi-database-down"></i> Download export (JSON)</button>
      </form>
    </div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="col-lg-5">
    <div class="panel"><div class="panel-body small">
      <h2 class="panel-title">Backups</h2>
      <p>Azure Cosmos DB also keeps its own automatic backups. You do not need to do anything for those.</p>
      <p class="mb-0">The download is logged in the audit trail. Keep exported files encrypted or in a locked location, as required by the Data Protection Act 2021.</p>
    </div></div>
  </div>
</div>
<%- include('../partials/footer') %>
